  "plain": "Families were picked for a secret programme in the 1960s partly by demographics, because its planners knew a certain share of the children would want to join the military. That is how a former sergeant named Dan Sherman, who says the NSA hired him to communicate with aliens, puts it to Michels, passing on what an officer he calls Captain White told him. If true, it would mean the programme chose families with an eye to their children's later careers."
